      "text": "All we have to do is add fractions. The easiest way to add fractions is to get the same denominator. In order to do this, we can multiply the fraction by $\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 + 5i}$, which works as the denominator has no $($s as the denominator.\n\\[\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i} + \\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i} = \\frac{(3 + 5i)(3 + 5i)}{(3 - 5i)(3 + 5i)} + \\frac{(3 - 5i)(3 - 5i)}{(3 + 5i)(3 - 5i)}.\\]Now, we can simplify the denominator as $3^2 - (5i)^2 = 9 - 25i^2.$ But since $i^2$ is the same as $-1,$ we have $9 - 25(-1) = 34.$ Now we can simplify the top. Note that $3^2 + (5i)^2 - (3^2 - (5i)^2) = 3^2 + (5i)^2 - 3^2 + (5i)^2 = 0.$ Therefore, our final answer is $\\frac{0}{34}.$\n\\[\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i}\\cdot \\frac{3 + 5i}{3 + 5i}\\ + \\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i}\\cdot \\frac{3 - 5i}{3 - 5i}\\ = \\frac{(3 + 5i )^2}{(3 + 5i)(3 - 5i)}\\ +\\ \\frac{(3 - 5i )^2}{(3 + 5i)(3 - 5i)}.\\]\nWe have \\[\\frac{(3 + 5i )^2 + (3 - 5i )^2}{(3 + 5i)(3 - 5i)} = \\frac{9 + 25\\textbf{i} + (25)\\textbf{i}^2 + 9 - 25\\textbf{i} + (25)\\textbf{i}^2}{(3 + 5i)(3 - 5i)}.\\]Simplifying the top, we get \\[\\frac{(9 + 9) + (25 - 25)\\textbf{i} + (-\\textbf{i}^2)\\cdot 50}{(3 + 5i)(3 - 5i)} = \\frac{18 + (50)\\textbf{i}}{34}.\\]Thus, our desired answer is  \\[\\frac{18 + 50i}{34}.\\]",
