      "text": "To simplify the expression \n\n\\[\n\\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i} + \\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i},\n\\]\n\nwe will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Define the complex numbers:**\n   Let \\(z_1 = \\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i}\\) and \\(z_2 = \\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i}\\).\n\n2. **Find the conjugates of \\(z_1\\) and \\(z_2\\):**\n   The conjugate of a complex number \\(a + bi\\) is \\(a - bi\\). Thus:\n   \\[\n   \\overline{z_1} = \\frac{3 - 5i}{3 + 5i}, \\quad \\overline{z_2} = \\frac{3 + 5i}{3 - 5i}.\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply the numerators and denominators by the conjugate:**\n   Multiply the numerator and denominator of \\(z_1\\) by \\(\\overline{z}_1\\):\n   \\[\n   z_1 \\cdot \\overline{z_1} = \\frac{(3 + 5i)}{(3 - 5i)} \\cdot \\frac{(3 + 5i)}{(3 + 5i)} = \\frac{(3 + 5i)^2}{(3 - 5i)(3 + 5i)}.\n   \\]\n\n4. **Simplify the denominator:**\n   \\[\n   (3 - 5i)(3 + 5i) = 3^2 - (5i)^2 = 9 - 25i^2 = 9 + 25 = 34.\n   \\]\n   Hence,\n   \\[\n   \\overline{z_1} = \\frac{(3 + 5i)^2}{34}.\n   \\]\n\n   Similarly, find \\(\\overline{z}_2\\):\n   \\[\n   z_2 \\cdot \\overline{z}_2 = \\frac{(3 - 5i)}{(3 + 5i)} \\cdot \\frac{(3 - 5i)}{(3 - 5i)} = \\frac{(3 - 5i)^2}{(3 + 5i)(3 - 5i)}.\n   \\]\n   Simplifying the denominator:\n   \\[\n   (3 + 5i)(3 - 5i) = 3^2 - (5i)^2 = 9 + 25 = 34.\n   \\]\n   Hence,\n   \\[\n   \\overline{z_2} = \\frac{(3 - 5i)^2}{34}.\n   \\]\n\n5. **Add the two conjugate results:**\n   \\[\n   \\frac{(3 + 5i)^2}{34} + \\frac{(3 - 5i)^2}{34}.\n   \\]\n\n6. **Simplify the numerator:**\n   Calculate \\((3 + 5i)^2\\) and \\((3 - 5i)^2\\):\n   \\[\n   (3 + 5i)^2 = 9 + 30i + 25i^2 = 9 + 30i - 25 = -16 + 30i,\n   \\]\n   since \\(i^2 = -1\\). Similarly,\n   \\[\n   (3 - 5i)^2 = 9 - 30i + 25i^2 = 9 - 30i - 25 = -16 - 30i.\n   \\]\n\n   Now sum them up:\n   \\[\n   -16 + 30i + (-16 - 30i) = -16 - 16 = -32.\n   \\]\n\n7. **Combine the result with the denominator:**\n   \\[\n   \\frac{-32}{34} = -\\frac{16}{17}.\n   \\]\n\n### Conclusion:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-\\frac{16}{17}}\n\\]",
